Z||000000||yo_sweet||12-13-2001||10:21 PM||||Went to canadian tire with the gilfriend last week end found a dual cup holder even has a flap that pop's down for food!, anyway with a bit of imagination i cut a small outlet hole in the top just a little notch to fit the closure on the middle console so now it sits nicely in the middle  without bothering any comfort and it works well! will get pics up soon i think you'll like wha you see and i would higly recommend this to anyone<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">  <P><BR>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html<BR>yo_sweet!||||reg||1
Z||000001||I wish I had a GT||12-13-2001||10:46 PM||||Hey when you get the pictures e-mail me, I've been thinking about doing that for some time now!!!<P>------------------<BR>**I wish I had a GT**||||reg||1
Z||000002||Blacktree||12-14-2001||02:46 AM||||Is a cupholder really THAT RARE in a Fiero? I have a cheapie cupholder in my daily driver. I have an aftermarket receiver (single-DIN height) which leaves 1" of open space above the receiver. And it just so happens that this cupholder was designed to fit in that 1" of open space. Check it out.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.tweaktech.com/temp-pic/f87cupholder1.jpg">  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.tweaktech.com/temp-pic/f87cupholder2.jpg">  <P>There is one small problem with this cupholder, though. If you have an automatic transmission like my daily driver does, the cupholder will not open all the way when you have the transmission in Park (it interferes with the shifter handle). Drop it into Reverse or Neutral and the cupholder opens all the way. The shifters in manual transmissions don't interfere with it.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A><p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
