Z||000005||Nashco||12-14-2001||12:06 PM||||It would only get on the radio face if you were accelerating backwards very fast! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Bryce<BR> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/nashcosig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||12-14-2001||01:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Blacktree:<BR><B>Is a cupholder really THAT RARE in a Fiero? I have a cheapie cupholder in my daily driver. I have an aftermarket receiver (single-DIN height) which leaves 1" of open space above the receiver. And it just so happens that this cupholder was designed to fit in that 1" of open space. Check it out.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tweaktech.com/temp-pic/f87cupholder1.jpg">   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tweaktech.com/temp-pic/f87cupholder2.jpg">   <P>There is one small problem with this cupholder, though. If you have an automatic transmission like my daily driver does, the cupholder will not open all the way when you have the transmission in Park (it interferes with the shifter handle). Drop it into Reverse or Neutral and the cupholder opens all the way. The shifters in manual transmissions don't interfere with it.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Pretty slick, but would it work under the radio?  That way you don't have as much of a problem with condensation dripping on the radio.  You can't access the radio either way - big disadvantage!||||reg||1
Z||000007||REDHOTT88||12-14-2001||01:38 PM||||The over the radio cupholder is coool!<P>It shouldn't matter that you can't open it in Park, because you should either be done with your drink, or leaving the vehicle with it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>More info please on ingredients!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over, runs smooth, shifts crisp!)</FONT>||||reg||1
