Z||000010||Blacktree||12-15-2001||02:05 AM||||First, let me explain that I've had this cupholder (and the stereo) for almost 4 years. I can't remember the name of the company I ordered it from, and no longer have the invoice. But I'm guessing that this info can be had wihtout too much trouble.<P>You see, when I first installed the stereo in the car (the 86 coupe), I used an aftermarket stereo installation kit bought from Pep Boys. In the instruction manual was a small pamphlet with some of the company's other products listed. One of those products was a cupholder designed to fit in the place of a graphic equalizer (like if you were to put a single-DIN stereo into a 1.5-DIN opening). <P>It just so happens the company's address was in there, too. So I sent them a letter asking about the cupholder. They mailed me back with an order form, the price, and the part number. I think it cost something like $12 including shipping.<P>Maybe if I were to stop by Pep Boys again, I could find one of these stereo install kits and copy down the address for yaz.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Regarding condensation... it's hard to tell in the pics, but the cupholder (when fully extended) holds the drinks about 1.5"-2" away from the face of the radio. VERY RARELY do any liquids get on the face of my stereo, and when it does happen it's usually the result of something spilling all over the place. But if you look at the pics you can see the water marks where water has dripped onto the console.<P>Regarding under-the-radio mounting... it won't work. I tried it. First of all, the little support that flips down to hold the bottom of the drink would have to be removed. Second of all, the cupholder would be practically sitting on the console, allowing drinks to tip more easily. And third of all, the cupholder cannot be fully extended because it hits the lip on the front of the center console piece.<P>Somehow I get the feeling that I ended up hijacking <B>Yo_sweet</B>'s thread. But I'm still hoping to see pics of his cupholder.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Blacktree||12-15-2001||02:53 AM||||<B>One last photo</B><P>This one will help illiustrate how the cupholder overlaps the center console piece and shifter base. In this pic, the shifter is in Neutral.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.tweaktech.com/temp-pic/f87cupholder3.jpg"> <P>Now it's time to go beddy-bye  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||yo_sweet||12-15-2001||03:38 AM||||it looks great but iw anted mine where there would be very little interfearance when it came to driving or just being comfterable, when i get pics i will post!...<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">  <P><BR>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html<BR>yo_sweet!||||reg||1
