Z||000014||Patrick's Dad||12-15-2001||10:44 AM||||A long time ago, before I was a Fiero owner, I was selling HiFi, including car stereo. I sold a system to a guy who owned a brand new Fiero. I didn't have the amp in stock, but I found out when and where he was having it installed. I ran to one of the other locations, grabbed the amp, and drove it over.<P>I've never forgotten one interesting thing that they did, and will probably do to mine, whether I keep the stock dash or get the PISA wraparound dash: They flipped the console bezel upside down and moved the tubing and wires, placing the radio on top, the vents on the bottom , and the HVAC slightly lower than they are. This might allow this cupholder to work better with the autostick.<P>My only problem with this cupholder is that it blocks the radio. I switch stations like crazy.<P>As an alternative, one could switch the bezel only, placing the DIN radio in the vent openings, moving the HVAC control slightly, and putting the cupholder below the actual vents. This, of course, would allow you to use the A/C to keep cold drinks cold, and the heater to keep hot drinks hot....||||reg||1
